  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Honeywell International shows $257M in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date. The Department of Defense obligated $257M for the period; the National Aeronautics and Space Administration shows $0. Obligations fell 58.9% year over year. Award activity for FY2026 to date totals 208 awards with an average award size of $1.2M. Military Armored Vehicle, Tank, and Tank Component Manufacturing is the largest market by obligations at $153M. Aircraft Manufacturing follows at $81.6M, and Aircraft Engine and Engine Parts Manufacturing records $14.1M. Other listed markets include Engineering Services at $3.7M and Turbine and Turbine Generator Set Units Manufacturing at $3.2M. Historical obligations by fiscal year show FY21 $437M, FY22 $536M, FY23 $489M, FY24 $696M, FY25 $626M, and FY26 $257M. This snapshot covers partial current-year totals for FY2026 to date and summarizes where federal spending landed for the period shown.",
